WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.540
Picture an air route between two cities,

2
00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:05.100
flown by just one airline.

3
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.680
No rival on the route.

4
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.120
Surely it can charge whatever it likes?

5
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.850
Yet some firms with large market
shares still keep their prices low.

6
00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:16.400
How can a firm with no rivals still act

7
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.850
as if it had them?

8
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.520
In this mission, you'll
test how high a lone

9
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.420
firm's price can go, in a graph lab.

10
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:26.070
Then you'll see why real
air routes don't always

11
00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.550
behave as the theory predicts.

12
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.880
Your mission: find out
whether one firm on its own

13
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.510
can still behave like it has competitors.
